"explanation": "In the modern antiretroviral era, patients with HIV who are adherent to therapy have near-normal life expectancy, and their leading cause of death has shifted from opportunistic infections to non-AIDS conditions. Cardiovascular disease (A) is the greatest risk because HIV itself and certain antiretroviral drugs (especially older PIs and NRTIs) accelerate atherosclerosis, and this patient is 42 years old with a high viral load now being treated. Opportunistic infections (E) are unlikely with ART-mediated CD4 preservation; HIV-related malignancies (C) are reduced by immune reconstitution.",
