"explanation": "This woman has chronic insomnia with identifiable behavioral contributors: late-night smoking (nicotine is a stimulant), irregular sleep-wake schedule, and using waking hours for housework rather than returning to sleep. There is no depression or anxiety to treat pharmacologically. Sleep hygiene education (A) is the appropriate initial step, addressing stimulus control, consistent sleep schedule, and avoiding stimulants near bedtime. Zolpidem (E) is not first-line for chronic insomnia and would not address the underlying behavioral drivers; pharmacotherapy for depression (B, C) is not indicated without a depressive disorder.",
