"explanation": "A 45-year-old woman with 1 year of amenorrhea, consistent condom use, and no medications most likely has primary ovarian insufficiency or natural menopause, and the confirming lab is FSH. Option B is correct because FSH is elevated (typically >40 mIU/mL) in menopause due to loss of ovarian negative feedback on the pituitary. Estradiol (A) can be low but is less specific and more variable; beta-hCG (C) would rule out pregnancy but not confirm menopause.",
