"explanation": "A 67-year-old man with syncope, dizziness, and hypotension with a pulse of 60/min has an ECG showing Mobitz type II second-degree AV block, which presents with intermittent non-conducted P waves without progressive PR prolongation. Option D is correct because Mobitz type II is characterized by constant PR intervals with sudden dropped QRS complexes, reflecting infranodal conduction disease with risk of complete heart block and requiring pacemaker placement. Mobitz type I (C, Wenckebach) shows progressive PR prolongation before the dropped beat and is generally more benign.",
